# local tool state. The cache and the generated critiques are throwaway, but
# .impeccable/config.json is not: it records deliberate, Deon-approved design
# decisions (why a given detector finding is a false positive here). Ignoring
# the whole folder meant those decisions lived on one machine only, so a fresh
# clone re-flagged brand devices that had already been signed off. Track the
# config, keep the rest local.
.impeccable/*
!.impeccable/config.json
dist/
dist-inlined/
.verify-shots/
metro.log

# demo/preview real photos — never commit family PII
assets/demo/
# built web export
dist/
.netlify/

# Security audit reports: detailed, exploitable vulnerability maps of this app.
# The GitHub repo (123Apathy/afterlight) is PUBLIC, so these must never be
# committed while that remains true. Kept locally only.
docs/RED-TEAM-*.md
